    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-02-2019-june/q4",
      "question": "<p>The infinite series <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm C\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm S\"></span> are defined by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm C=\\cos\\theta+\\frac12\\cos 5\\theta+\\frac14\\cos 9\\theta+\\frac18\\cos 13\\theta+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm S=\\sin\\theta+\\frac12\\sin 5\\theta+\\frac14\\sin 9\\theta+\\frac18\\sin 13\\theta+\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>Given that the series <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm C\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm S\"></span> are both convergent,</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm C+\\mathrm i\\mathrm S=\\frac{2\\mathrm e^{\\mathrm i\\theta}}{2-\\mathrm e^{4\\mathrm i\\theta}}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>Hence show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm S=\\frac{4\\sin\\theta+2\\sin 3\\theta}{5-4\\cos 4\\theta}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
