      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-02-2019-june/q6",
      "question": "<p>In an Argand diagram, the points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> are the vertices of an equilateral triangle with its centre at the origin. The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> represents the complex number <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6+2\\mathrm i\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Find the complex numbers represented by the points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>, giving your answers in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x+\\mathrm iy\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span> are real and exact. <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li></ol><p>The points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"E\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"F\"></span> are the midpoints of the sides of triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>Find the exact area of triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"DEF\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
