      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-02-2019-june/q7",
      "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M=\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;-1&amp;1\\\\3&amp;k&amp;4\\\\3&amp;2&amp;-1\\end{pmatrix}\\qquad\\text{where }k\\text{ is a constant}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> for which the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M\"></span> has an inverse. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Find, in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span>, the coordinates of the point where the following planes intersect<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z&amp;=p\\\\3x-6y+4z&amp;=1\\\\3x+2y-z&amp;=0\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span> for which the set of simultaneous equations<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z&amp;=1\\\\3x-5y+4z&amp;=q\\\\3x+2y-z&amp;=0\\end{aligned}\" data-display=\"true\"></div>can be solved.</li><li>For this value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span>, interpret the solution of the set of simultaneous equations geometrically. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol></li></ol>",
